    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "Draft (≈ 760 characters):\n\n> I am the first author of \"TutorTrace,\" a full paper accepted to ACM UIST 2026, the premier venue for user interface systems research. I will present the paper in the \"Learning & Tutoring\" session on October 7, 2026. The work was conducted in Dr. Yan Chen's PRIME Lab at Virginia Tech and is based on a deployment in CS 3114, so the presentation directly represents VT research and the department's work on computing education. Presenting in person allows me to answer questions from the community, connect with researchers working on instructor-facing tools, and gather feedback for follow-up studies. Funding will cover registration and part of the travel costs.\n\nOn the leave of absence: that probably *does* matter. Many travel-funding programs require enrollment during the term of travel. Ask Grace Kim before submitting whether a student on approved leave is eligible, and whether the advisor's grant can cover it instead."
     ]
    },
